<title>NETHERLANDS: Wegener splits shares one for five.</title>
<headline>Wegener splits shares one for five.</headline>
<dateline>APELDOORN, Netherlands 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch publisher Wegener NV said on Wednesday it proposed to split its shares on a one for five basis.</p>
<p>The company earlier posted 1996 net profit of 69.4 million guilders, up from 58.7 million a year earlier.  </p>
<p>In a statement accompanying the results, Wegener gave no reason for the share split.</p>
<p>The shares closed on Tuesday at 190.50 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
